questions.question:
The new filter and how it is registered:

// common/domain-error.filter.ts
@Catch(DomainError)
export class DomainErrorFilter implements ExceptionFilter {
  catch(error: DomainError, host: ArgumentsHost) {
    // maps the error and writes an application/problem+json response
  }
}

// main.ts
app.useGlobalFilters(new DomainErrorFilter());

Server log:
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'plan')
    at EnrollmentsService.enroll (enrollments.service.ts:57:31)

Response to the client:
HTTP/1.1 500 Internal Server Error
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8

{"statusCode":500,"message":"Internal server error"}

Statement: "This response was written by Nest's built-in exception filter, not by DomainErrorFilter, because @Catch(DomainError) only receives DomainError instances."

